This repository adapts files from other projects. Each adapted file keeps a header that
names its origin and its license and says that it was modified. The list below gives
each file, its origin, its license and the changes made to it.


skill-creator
  Origin:  https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official, plugins/skill-creator,
           plugin cache fa59bc903774
  License: Apache License, Version 2.0; the upstream holds no NOTICE file.

  domains/skill-tooling/skills/authoring-skills/scripts/viewer.py
    From plugins/skill-creator/skills/skill-creator/eval-viewer/generate_review.py.
    Changes:
    - Reads an iteration as workspace.py, run.py, grade.py and benchmark.py write it —
      iteration.json, eval_metadata.json, run.json, response.md, changes.json,
      grading.json, benchmark.json, feedback.json — rather than any folder that holds an
      outputs/ folder.
    - Reads output files at their paths under outputs/, each shown as text when it reads
      as UTF-8, rather than by a list of extensions; the xlsx and pdf renderings are left
      out.
    - Escapes every `<` of the embedded data, so that no output can close the page's
      script.
    - Embeds the iteration's reviews, keys them by run name, and checks a review's shape
      and run before writing it.
    - Leaves a port in use to its process and takes a free one, where the original
      killed the process listening on it; opens no browser.

  domains/skill-tooling/skills/authoring-skills/assets/viewer.html
    From plugins/skill-creator/skills/skill-creator/eval-viewer/viewer.html.
    Changes:
    - Loads nothing from the network: the Google Fonts and the SheetJS script are left
      out, system fonts in their place.
    - Shows for each run its name, expected output, status, figures, closing account and
      deleted files, and the case's review items beside the feedback box.
    - Reads grading.json's assertions, weak assertions and checked claims.
    - Renders benchmark.py's benchmark.json: each metric's statistics with the delta, the
      pass rate by case, the runs with their cost, models and efforts, the assertions,
      and the notes.
    - Keys the feedback by run name, and says where to put the feedback.json a static
      page downloads; its texts address the agent.
